+# T10: abandoned forms must not use up the 50 unfinished drafts (C2-008)
+
+Model: Sonnet, medium effort. BASE: 6aea8e5230e6e32ce8070b0e9cd3b351570f6e02.
+
+## Cause
+`submissions.new()` refuses at `MAX_OPEN = 50` unsealed folders; only the 24-hour `STALE_SECONDS` sweep removes
+abandoned ones. The page makes a draft per form (`POST /api/submissions`) and the service has no route to release
+one (`service.py` is outside this task's files), so the page cannot release its draft.
+
+## Repair (service only, `submissions.py`)
+At the ceiling, `new()` first removes the oldest drafts idle for `IDLE_SECONDS` (2 hours), as many as needed, then
+refuses if still full. Never removed: a sealed (submitted) folder (not counted open at all), a draft with an
+upload in flight, a draft with an `issued` approval (it reached the review), any draft touched in the last 2 hours.
+`reading()` now touches the draft, as uploads and removals already do, so a form that is reading its documents is
+live. Submit's idempotence is unchanged (sealed/issued records are not touched). The limit stays at 50 and still
+refuses when 50 drafts are live. Why this and not a page change: no delete route exists and the page cannot be
+changed without one; counting liveness by idle time needs no new surface and only acts when the limit is hit.
+Residual: a form idle for over 2 hours at the limit, before reaching the review, can lose its draft (then
+"unknown submission"); a drafts that reached the review are kept until the 24-hour sweep.
+
+## Files
+`src/deploy_workflow/run_start/submissions.py`, `tests/test_run_start_submissions.py`, walk under `output/5-repair/T10/`.
+
+## Tests
+Five new tests at the end of `tests/test_run_start_submissions.py` (abandoned draft makes room; recent draft kept;
+issued draft kept; upload in flight kept; reading keeps a draft live). Before: 5 failed (no `IDLE_SECONDS`).
+After: `pytest -q tests/test_run_start_submissions.py tests/test_run_start_scheduler.py tests/test_run_start_service.py
+tests/test_react_frontend.py`: 430 passed, 3 skipped. No existing test changed.
+
+## Probe p22 (output, C2_PORT=8750)
+Exit 0 before and after. It makes 50 fresh drafts in seconds, so none is idle: after the repair it still prints
+`"alerts": ["too many unfinished submissions; try again later"]` (correct, 50 live drafts). It cannot show the
+repair, so a walk was saved: `T10/walk-abandoned-drafts.cjs` (50 drafts, all but two aged 3 hours; one fresh, one
+with an `issued` file). Base: exit 1, `FAIL the form reaches Purpose with 50 abandoned drafts [["too many
+unfinished submissions; try again later"]]` (`T10/before-walk.txt`). Repair: exit 0, all five checks ok, fresh and
+issued drafts kept, count 50 (`T10/after-walk.txt`).
+
+## Gates
+`quality_gate.py --base BASE`: 0 findings (one E501 fixed first). T07 walk-leave-and-return, walk-carried-work and
+T08 walk-t08: exit 0, no FAIL. T09 walk-issuer-id: no FAIL lines. No web file changed, so the web gates and vitest
+were not re-run.
+
+Not verified: the T09 walk's exit code itself (only its FAIL count); behaviour under concurrent Submit during
+eviction (both run under `_LOCK`; not stress-tested); web gates (no web change).
